Subject: [PATCH] mmc: dw_mmc: fall back to PIO when DMA re-init fails on resume

On the A12 the PL330 DMA engine can fail ('Runtime PM usage count
underflow', 'pl330_update ... Unexpected!'). dw_mci_runtime_resume then
gets no external DMA channel, edmac_init leaves host->dms NULL and returns
an error, yet use_dma stays EDMAC; the card reset path oopsed in
dw_mci_edmac_start_dma (pstore before boot f8f51dd6) and stop_dma (test 22).
Switch to PIO instead so an SD error does not become a kernel panic.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -3464,8 +3464,13 @@
 
 	if (host->use_dma && host->dma_ops->init) {
 		ret = host->dma_ops->init(host);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+		if (ret) {
+			/* A failed channel request leaves host->dms NULL; staying in
+			 * DMA mode would dereference it on the next transfer.
+			 */
+			dev_warn(host->dev, "DMA re-init failed (%d), using PIO\n", ret);
+			host->use_dma = TRANS_MODE_PIO;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/*
